            <ArticleTitle>Overestimation of impairment-related asthma control by adolescents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1028-1030.e1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jpeds.2011.01.034</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We investigated the concordance between adolescents' perceived and impairment-related asthma control. Based on self-reported medication use, symptoms, and activity limitations, most overestimated their impairment-related control (73.8%). Providers should ask detailed, structured questions to get the most comprehensive picture of a patient's impairment-related control so they can ultimately improve disease outcomes.</AbstractText>
